==Battleground==
*The enemy base is protected by a [[Base Barrier]] until the boss is defeated.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Li'l Bun Bun]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*3 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Xenobeast Bunaglios]] spawns as the boss.
**4 [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s spawn, delay 50~53.33 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,600f</sup>.
**8 [[Mooth]]s spawn, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
**Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 86.67~100 seconds<sup>2,600f~3,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Teacher Bun Bun]] spawns after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This is likely the hardest of the four stages, as now you're facing off against a plethora of [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating Enemies]] with buffed Sir Rels as support. To deal with Xenobeast Bunaglios, the same tankers, [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]], maintain their regular usage. The difficulty mainly comes from the Teacher Bun Bun, whose inflated stats combined with Xenobeast Bunaglios killing your normal counters creates some insane pushing power. [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] is extremely good here, being able to deal massive damage to the Li'l Bun Buns as well as being able to chip away at the Teacher Bun Bun. As for the Sir Rels, it is important to dispose of them quickly, as letting them stack up will make them extremely difficult to handle. Thankfully, they don't have a lot of health even at their 150% buff, so disposing of them is not a high order. While there are Mooths in this level, not only are they annoyingly hard to reach, they aren't infinite, meaning you shouldn't take the cash for granted and should focus on dealing as much damage as possible before your cash supply drains up. Either try to snipe the Mooths with Cyberpunk, an Uber, or pray that your Jelly Dumplings get enough [[Wave Attack|Waves]] off to kill each Mooth.

If you don't have any suitable [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]], the most viable strategy for King of the Beasts III stacking is [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] stacking given how much pure power this stage throws at you. As such, it is highly recommended that you bring Cyberpunk. Another completely different strategy is to bring [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Soractes]] to weaken Xenobeast Bungalios with his Summoner, then use with high DPS anti-Alien or Behemoth units like [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] and [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] to do as much damage to Xenobeast Bunaglios as possible the instant he spawns, taking advantage of the 53 second delay between Bungalios and Bun Bun spawning.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]: A vital unit to knock out Teacher Bun Bun quickly, as well as to deal with the Li'l Bun Buns before they pose too much of a threat.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: As usual, Can Can proves to be an insane unit: dealing high damage to Li'l Bun Bun and Sir Rel, and being able to hit Xenobeast Bunaglios during his time between attacks.
*[[Miter Saw Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Saw Cat]]: A strong [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] that can rack up good damage at the start of the battle. Loses much of his usage after Teacher Bun Bun spawns, though.
*[[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]]: Like in the rest of Xenobeast Bunaglios' stages, Soap is a excellent unit to use against Xenobeast Bunaglios to try and wall him. Its decently high base HP lets it work some magic even after Teacher Bun Bun joins the battle.
*[[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]]: Tanker able to give temporary relief to Xenobeast Bunaglios' super-high damage. Note that he will melt really fast against Teacher Bun Bun, so don't rely on him too much.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: A strong unit who can distract the enemies present here for a few seconds.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Powerful disposable unit that simplifies the startoff, and can heavily damage both the Li'l Bun Buns and the Mooths.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk]]: The main hardcarrier of your runs for this stage if you lack good Ubers. His extremely high range and Slow allow him to reduce the potential pushing power of both bosses. It is highly advised to try and stack at least two of them before hitting the base.
*[[Killer Cat (Rare Cat)|Radical Cat]]: Provided he's boosted to Lv.50, he can actually be of use here. His Strong Against gives him ''155,250'' health against Teacher Bun Bun, Li'l Bun Bun and Mooth, and thanks to Behemoth Slayer, he has a decent ''103,500'' health against Bunaglios. His base health isn't bad either, with 62,100 health for a unit that can be spawned every 6 seconds. Beware that he can be a little expensive to spam, especially alongside Soap Cat.
*[[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Catcrates]]: The core of rush strategies that aim to burst Bunaglios as soon as he spawns, his Conjure ability helps provide a consistent, reliable weaken proc against Bunaglios for your stack of units to survive and rack up more damage.
*[[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]]: A strong choice on rush strategies. Their Behemoth Slayer allows them to do good damage to Bunaglios, while helping relieve the pressure asserted by the Sir Rels. They also help snipe down the Mooths to help gather cash.
*[[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]]: Royal Guard Cat's immense Anti-Alien DPS is important for rush strategies. At level 50, each Royal Guard Cat can do an insane '''34k''' damage per second against Bungalios.
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]: An alternative to Radical Cat to stall the Floating enemies, most notably Teacher Bun Bun for a cheaper price. Do note that she is much worse against Bunaglios and thus is mainly used for rush strategies, where Bunaglios would've been severely weakened and surviving Teacher Bun Bun becomes more important.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Assassinlan Pasalan]]: A unit similar to Cyberpunk who not only possesses a guaranteed Slow with high range, but also lacks a blind spot. If you happen to have a free slot, you can also Combo him with [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]] to gain a medium Slow Combo, further improving his performance.
*[[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle/Stroller]]: Disposable Uber who can dish out some crazy damage. Their strong Wave allows their attacks to reach Mooths as well, which could otherwise be major annoyances. If you happen to have Cats in the Cradle's [[Ultra Form]], they become even stronger here, minimizing their odds of wasting a hit and extending their Wave level.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]]: Cosmo's Ultra Form is extremely strong on this level, having high enough range to stand outside Xenobeast's Explosion and having a ridiculously strong wave that not only clears all peons, but can Freeze all Floating enemies present here. True Form also works here, albeit with less power, as Cosmo's True Form lacks a Level 10 Wave.
*[[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Eclipsed]]: An amazing tanker, being able to stall Xenobeast Bunaglios, Teacher Bun Bun, the Lil Bun Buns and the Mooths all in one. Lunos' health is also good enough to stall the Sir Rels momentarily, albeit for a very short time, as he gets shredded. His Conjure can pick off Sir Rels easily and snipe Mooths, as well as give a plethora of cash thanks to double bounty.
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Netherworld Nymph Lunacia]]: Despite not targeting the biggest threat here, she targets the second most dangerous enemy: Teacher Bun Bun. Her [[Weaken]], high bulk and good damage allows her to be an amazing counter against Bun Bun, not to mention she will shred through the Li'l Bun Buns and Mooths. Her Explosions Immunity allows her to be on the battlefield for longer periods, and she has a fairly quick cooldown and cheap cost, which allows for a second Lunacia to be spawned after the first one dies. After Bun Bun is dead, Xenobeast is nothing but a punching bag for your general counters to thrive against.

